{"title":"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A lattice point in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate system is any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> where both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers. The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfb1b8f564901dd14ad70a5e2c937ea9d8c5428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx +2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> passes through no lattice point with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c8a55111e91443ac56a007fee9cadeab1774f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x \\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab24211e8c6cd92bef80e95ecf7d45d23afcc10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} &lt; m &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />. What is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e328f743d2fef01d1e41b4012f4e4d416daefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{51}{101} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{50}{99} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{51}{100} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{52}{101} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{13}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"440\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1bd9e9a2a82d0af53d34252ca77ddb9f5b0b76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> to not pass through any lattice points with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f6bce98091845a86f93d5471a93240e5b5e38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> is the same as saying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6fcd5f085db28aae1117dc2e9276d9a987c5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$mx\\notin\\mathbb Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87d80c513bb7186f22ba4c6ce94539d667338a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\{1,2,\\dots,100\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, or in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not expressible as a ratio of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70be6995b09baf8d0976d9f17955aa88d98dd8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s/t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f50c33941635f92564e7e6f61e297a8d08fa24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />. Hence the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first real number after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> that is so expressible.\n</p><p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62c84c1d5ee8e435ad5bdf2dcf2d8d9d9ecaca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=2,\\dots,100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />, the smallest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f473e84d04440b4f694f931eec597fa6baa85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> which exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24d885338618a73595d668a9eb70e227fda5a829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,\\frac23,\\frac34,\\frac35,\\dots,\\frac{50}{98},\\frac{50}{99},\\frac{51}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" /> respectively, and the smallest of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c7ec89bd9e66292341e5ff6bdea14daabf3f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\frac{50}{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that finding the next possible slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is the same as finding the next Farey fraction of order <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Hence, we can use the Farey mediant theorem (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farey_sequence#Farey_neighbours\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farey_sequence#Farey_neighbours</a>), which states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69508d506a4b48d59875bcdf0e885b2e2f566235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}&lt;\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"33\" /> are neighboring Farey fractions of order <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c99119ecfd4db7271d00c4cb6c165842a94f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc-ad=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/4902072d94478dca658238b03fa24d3f93e16c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, d \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df1c3345e0c42d0533da069c3cd528db94d17142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c-d=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. We try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69ceed5aab8792777e7625777efdf5452cfe82f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, but that doesn't give integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. We try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1018997c89ab9c09ed3239e0211f4132a71fc917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/6168f940658a40f1e5ede3bc722b33d8691ca8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> so the upper bound is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c7ec89bd9e66292341e5ff6bdea14daabf3f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\frac{50}{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~Math-lover1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that for the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1bd9e9a2a82d0af53d34252ca77ddb9f5b0b76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> to not pass through any lattice points, the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, or else it would be canceled by some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d46b7fb3a219ebe7d2bc57de37798c8f830ec8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\le100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> which would make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> an integer. By using common denominators, we find that the order of the fractions from smallest to largest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2369a7eadc93f664e0fe8aced85c26049d25eb01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A), (B), (C), (D), (E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" />. We can see that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8d830b1e730bed49a5717da164d9a079536824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> could be an integer, so therefore any fraction greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> would not work, as substituting our fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> would produce an integer for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. So now we are left with only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d75d57e066a182bb360075f72a27bad12f01ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd3326072e9f8e830356092a2da940625f3882d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{101}=\\frac{5049}{9999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eeef6b6cbf431dd38afdd8bbcb6f39555997f90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}=\\frac{5050}{9999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"37\" />, we can be absolutely certain that there isn't a number between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d75d57e066a182bb360075f72a27bad12f01ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> that can reduce to a fraction whose denominator is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Since we are looking for the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we take the larger of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d75d57e066a182bb360075f72a27bad12f01ed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c7ec89bd9e66292341e5ff6bdea14daabf3f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\frac{50}{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"62\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to find the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that there will be an integral solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1bd9e9a2a82d0af53d34252ca77ddb9f5b0b76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d46b7fb3a219ebe7d2bc57de37798c8f830ec8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\le100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. We first test A, but since the denominator has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be a nonzero multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, but it then will be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. We then test B. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755360e627531b196f8e870de39975e01f5ebbde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{50}{99}x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" /> yields the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/39326f6845950ec5c0ded5da67e6242fde7eb340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(99,52)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> which satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d46b7fb3a219ebe7d2bc57de37798c8f830ec8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\le100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Checking the answer choices, we know that the largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765f16b77312acd9f599cccdcd0459e2001f6cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}\\implies\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f7c0c752fadd1373f58dcec4fc1211c1a4f49b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2=\\frac{50}{100}x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0915cc1e4227db0c107c7feceaba36941f940c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=99$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is one of the integral values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd8f6fa8b19ffc095185ff102c5695b00686015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{100}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"38\" /> is the closest to its next integral value.\n</p><p><br />\nThus the maximum value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> when the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8d13524370f19d69a17666a2a0396c4b347791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=99m+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> goes through its next lattice point, which occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdf4ece0e68e600849230ea77982d6ace4fdc77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\frac{b}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFinding the common denominator, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2de1e4e330ee675e67c3dfe649acbe84a4ea042.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{50}{100}=\\frac{4950}{9900}, \\frac{b}{99}=\\frac{100b}{9900}\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea77deca157e5a7031617781221f872c54fc89d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />, the smallest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e854d3552d32b7f713b4ce323a5973199dbd0f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100b&gt;4950$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f95c60fbb990939840b5552bc3efd0b6a94df6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=50$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Thus the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8078b9c3c26552c260cf0d37becbeb73fb9ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}.\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f6bce98091845a86f93d5471a93240e5b5e38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, the nearest lattice point directly above the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe25f5f2a1b536e0582470503cca0c38a0b0211a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9dc1d45dcba8b061275ed817275ce1765599a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,\\frac{1}{2}x+3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae15b9b9dbf7fa2924840dc7d61b06e47e6d8569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. The slope of the line that contains this point and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0ef68f274ec95f4a8f94eebff49accdcf689ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b78d2075518654a293349127099eff0bd872327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921f9595111466f091924ad55fd54d4347c8190f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. The minimum value of the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/20226680c294b600ad18431ca70828c0191589f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{51}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b40301620472a97d6073256ff855fbd199130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{50}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. Therefore the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1bd9e9a2a82d0af53d34252ca77ddb9f5b0b76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=mx+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> contains no lattice point with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f6bce98091845a86f93d5471a93240e5b5e38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x\\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/4642a165426b9fe880469d604865f3d7e1d0fd2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}&lt;m&lt;\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\frac{50}{99}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"141\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~ Ning\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B\">2011 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145904\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 655/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19885/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.148      1 -total\n 61.74%    8.117      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 37.27%    4.900      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9482:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017145904 and revision id 289595. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}